  "response_text": "The thread\u2019s stack was set up by switching the current stack to our thread\u2019s stack, and then copying over the context. First, the stack pointer is changed set to our PSP. Then, decrementing the pointer each time, each register in that stack is set. xPSR and PC are set manually while the rest of the registers are set to arbitrary values. These register values are known as the context. The context is important for the thread to maintain its state, essentially setting it up as if it had always been running.\\n",
